Project Intelligence for yield-vault.wasm

## Code Patterns

### Storage Pattern
- Use StoragePointer::from_keyword("/key-name") for all persistent storage
- Follow the established naming convention for storage keys:
  - `/name` - Vault token name
  - `/symbol` - Vault token symbol
  - `/asset-name` - Underlying asset name
  - `/asset-symbol` - Underlying asset symbol
  - `/decimals` - Decimal precision
  - `/total-supply` - Total share supply tracking
  - `/total-assets` - Total assets under management
  - `/yield-rate` - Configured yield rate in basis points
  - `/last-yield-update` - Timestamp of last yield update
  - `/balances/{account}` - Account share balances
  - `/data/{key}` - Custom stored data
  - `/initialized` - Initialization guard

### Security Patterns
- Always call observe_initialization() in Initialize operation
- Use overflow_error() for all numeric operations to prevent overflow
- Validate transaction hash to prevent transaction replay attacks
- Implement check_authorization() to verify transaction permissions
- Update yield before any state-changing operation

### Implementation Patterns
- Use AlkaneResponder trait for message dispatching
- Follow ERC-4626 interface for yield-bearing vault functionality
- Group opcodes by functionality (initialization, asset management, view functions)
- Implement preview functions to simulate effects of operations
- Apply yield accrual that increases assets while maintaining same supply

## Opcode Standards
- 0: Initialize(name, symbol, asset_name, asset_symbol, decimal_offset)
- 10-19: Asset Management Operations
  - 10: Deposit(tx_hash, caller, receiver, assets)
  - 11: Mint(tx_hash, caller, receiver, shares)
  - 12: Withdraw(tx_hash, caller, receiver, owner, assets)
  - 13: Redeem(tx_hash, caller, receiver, owner, shares)
- 100-199: Metadata View Functions
  - 100: GetName() -> String
  - 101: GetSymbol() -> String
  - 102: GetDecimals() -> u8
  - 103: GetAsset() -> String
- 200-299: Accounting View Functions
  - 200: GetTotalAssets() -> u128
  - 201: ConvertToShares(assets) -> u128
  - 202: ConvertToAssets(shares) -> u128
- 300-399: Limit View Functions
  - 300: GetMaxDeposit(receiver) -> u128
  - 301: GetMaxMint(receiver) -> u128
  - 302: GetMaxWithdraw(owner) -> u128
  - 303: GetMaxRedeem(owner) -> u128
- 400-499: Preview View Functions
  - 400: PreviewDeposit(assets) -> u128
  - 401: PreviewMint(shares) -> u128
  - 402: PreviewWithdraw(assets) -> u128
  - 403: PreviewRedeem(shares) -> u128
- 500-599: Custom Data Operations
  - 500: SetData(key, value)
  - 501: GetData(key) -> String
- 600-699: Balance Management
  - 600: GetBalanceOf(account) -> u128
  - 601: GetTotalSupply() -> u128
- 900-999: Administrative Operations
  - 900: UpdateYield(yield_rate)

## Critical Implementation Paths

1. Initialization sequence:
   - Call observe_initialization() to prevent multiple initializations
   - Set token and asset metadata (name, symbol, asset name, asset symbol, decimals)
   - Initialize accounting state (total supply, total assets)
   - Initialize yield tracking (yield rate, last update timestamp)

2. Asset Management:
   - Validate transaction hash to prevent replay attacks
   - Update yield before state changes
   - Check limit constraints before operation
   - Convert between assets and shares at current exchange rate
   - Update balances and totals

3. Yield Accrual:
   - Calculate time elapsed since last update
   - Apply yield rate to total assets for the elapsed time
   - Update total assets while maintaining same total supply
   - Update last yield timestamp

## Project Preferences
- Use Rust 2021 edition
- Follow standard Rust naming conventions
- Use anyhow for error handling
- Implement comprehensive error messages
- Use checked arithmetic operations for all numeric calculations
- Document all public functions and interfaces

## Known Challenges
- Ensuring proper initialization guard is in place
- Preventing transaction replay attacks
- Handling precision issues in asset/share conversions
- Managing yield accrual calculations to avoid overflow
- Maintaining compatibility with the ERC-4626 standard while adapting to Bitcoin

## Tool Usage Patterns
- Use cargo for building and testing
- Compile to WebAssembly for deployment
- Use git for version control
- Build with blockchain feature enabled for production deployment
